   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to issuing \"West\nIndian American Day Carnival\" distinctive license plates",
    "basePrintNo": "S9012",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9012-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §404-ee, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S9012\n\nSPONSOR: PERSAUD\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to issuing\n\"West Indian American Day Carnival\" distinctive license plates\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide an opportunity for New Yorkers to show cultural pride in\ntheir West Indian heritage through the purchase of the distinctive West\nIndian American Day Carnival license plate.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill adds § 404-z to the vehicle and traffic law\nauthorizing the issuance of distinctive \"West Indian American Day Carni-\nval\" license plates. Subdivision one provides that any resident of New\nYork State to, upon request, be issued a distinctive \"West Indian Ameri-\ncan Day Carnival\" license plate of a design developed and approved by\nthe commissioner. Subdivision two provides that the distribution of a\n\"West Indian American Day Carnival\" license plate shall he issued in the\nsame manner as other number plates upon the payment of regular registra-\ntion fees and an additional annual $25.00 fee.\n\nSection two of the bill provides that a distinctive plate shall only be\ndesigned, produced, and issued upon the delivery of a surety bond in the\namount of $6,000 or at least 200 orders for such distinctive plate with\nthe additional one-time service charge applicable to each order.All of\nthe service charges will be deposited into the DMV distinctive place\ndevelopment fund. The language also provides that if after two years\nfollowing the date upon which the plate is first made available for\nsale, 200 or more sets of plates are sold, the bond shall be discontin-\nued. If fewer than 200 plates are sold within the first 2 years, the DMV\nshall be entitled to recover against the bond in the amount propor-\ntionate to the short fall.\n\nSection three of the bill provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe West Indian American Day Carnival takes place on Labor Day on East-\nern Parkway in Brooklyn and has generated significant revenue for New\nYork City and New York State. Many people from across the nation come to\nNew York City to take part in this celebration of cultural pride that is\njoyously displayed during the annual carnival and parade. The issuance\nof a license plate in recognition of this significant event which brings\nmore than a million people together each Labor Day is an appropriate\nrecognition of this auspicious cultural event.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2015-2016: A.6303 - Referred to Transportation\n2013-2014: A.4S39 - Referred to Transportation\n2011-2012: A.3089 - Referred to Transportation\n2010: A.3552/C.8266 - Referred to Transportation / Passed Senate\n2009: A.3552 - Referred to Transportation\n2007-2008: A.5158-A - Referred to Transportation\n2006: A.4055-B - Referred to Transportation\n2005: A.4055-A - Referred to Ways and Means\n2003-04: A.11095 - Referred to Transportation.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately, provided, however, that section one shall take effect one\nhundred eighty days after becoming a law. Effective immediately, the\naddition, amendment and/or repeal of any rule or regulation necessary\nfor the implementation of this act on its effective date are authorized\nand directed to be made and completed on or before such effective date.\n",
